From e6f887f783a49db7c5dda8783726dbc73806f8c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 05:07:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02272/11362] [outer-loop] build the LLM gap-filler: iGPU LLM
 writes a goal-distance heuristic for stalled games

The 'LLM is a gap-filler not solver' reframe, made concrete. arc_gap_fill.py: characterize a
stalled game (banked win-state + transitions) -> iGPU LLM writes ONE focused component, a
goal_distance(grid) heuristic (LOWER=closer to win) -> plug into the value-guided search
(graph_explore_solve_v3 verifier=) -> A/B vs novelty-only, reproduction-gated. The LLM writes
the small missing piece; the deterministic search solves. LocalGGUFProposer.generate() added
(generic required-funcs completion) + LLAMA_SERVER now prefers the ROCm iGPU HIP build (no
3090/conductor contention; 108GB unified fits even 35B).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
